description:
## Goal

Provide an explicit runtime-library validation request that catches unresolved callees in otherwise cold private clauses without changing ordinary demand-driven compilation.

A normal compile is correct to leave unreachable functions and clauses cold. This ticket must not make user compilation enumerate the runtime library or turn source presence into semantic demand.

## Final model

The validation front door requests one retained validation product for an exact runtime-library `SourceOwner`/version. Its membership comes from the source publication's typed, source-owned definition inventory. That product explicitly demands the ordinary scope/lowering/name-resolution facts for each published callable and retains their results through ProductMemo.

Each body is checked by the same jobs, resolver, `AttemptOutcome`, dependency ledger, and diagnostic provenance as an ordinarily reached body. The validation request is the demand edge; source name, module kind, compiler startup, queue drain, or global state is not.

Do not add an AST callee walker, second resolver, eager normal-compilation mode, runtime-module whitelist, source/World scan, diagnostic side channel, or duplicate validation cache.

## TDD

Prove:

- the runtime-library repro with `Kernel.no_such_function/1` fails the explicit validation request at the exact call provenance;
- the same cold function remains untouched during an ordinary unrelated user-root request;
- a valid library validates once and an identical request reuses the same retained product/allocation/generation with zero compiler work or deep copy;
- adding/removing/changing one library body invalidates only that body's exact validation dependents and aggregate product;
- rejected source replacement preserves the accepted validation result and provenance;
- independent source owners and unrelated edits move nothing;
- FIFO, LIFO, and permutation produce identical diagnostics and product identity.

## Ordering and acceptance

Implement only after fz-tfn.60 has proven the final source, fact, attempt, warning, provenance, and ProductMemo ownership model. This is a downstream explicit consumer, not a prerequisite or exception to that model.

Update runtime-library validation and compiler pipeline documentation. Remove all construction probes and fixtures not retained as durable public regressions. Full focused, causal, replacement, library, fixture, CLI, formatting, check, and strict-Clippy gates pass.
